    <div class="w-[10rem] mt-5 mb-6">
        <Image
            class="fill-current rounded-ac-md"
            format="webp"
            width={300}
            height={300}
            src={url('favicon.svg')}
            alt="icon"
        />
    </div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-3">About Me</div>

    <div class="mb-8 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed space-y-3">
        <p>
            Hi! I'm <span class="font-semibold">Jieyi Wang</span>, and you can
            call me <span class="font-semibold">Jinxy</span> ٩(◕‿◕)۶
        </p>
        <p>
            I study <span class="font-semibold">Mathematics and Computing</span>
            at <span class="font-semibold">Georgia Tech</span>. My focus is
            <span class="font-semibold">optimization</span> and
            <span class="font-semibold"
                >neuro-inspired computing for decision making</span
            >.I like figuring out how systems choose (｡•̀ᴗ-)✧
        </p>
        <p>
            My interest started in <span class="font-semibold">optimization</span
            >, then moved toward <span class="font-semibold">online learning</span
            >. Along the way, what I cared about shifted. The settings I like
            most are the ones where a system has to act under uncertainty, on
            limited observations. There, performance seemed to depend less on the
            update rule. It depended more on what the model assumed about how a
            decision unfolds over time ( •̀ ω •́ )✧
        </p>
        <p>
            That assumption is the part I keep coming back to. How does structure
            shape a choice? How does history carry into the next one? I'm just as
            curious about <span class="font-semibold">optimization</span> and
            <span class="font-semibold">decision making</span> as I was at the
            start, only now I ask better questions about them. I'd like to keep
            studying this for a long time (๑•̀ㅂ•́)و✧
        </p>

        <p>
            Outside of that, I paint. I'm also a little obsessed with
            architecture — floor plans, light, how a building quietly tells you
            where to walk. Painting taught me to look before judging. Buildings
            taught me that good structure feels effortless. Both show up in how
            I think about math ପ(๑•ᴗ•๑)ଓ
        </p>
        <p>
           Feel free to reach out — I'm always happy to Connect (｡･ω･｡)ﾉ♡
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-3">Contact</div>

    <ul class="mb-8 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-none">
        <li>
            <span class="opacity-70">School</span>
            <a class="email-link" href="mailto:jieyi.wang@gatech.edu">
                jieyi.wang@gatech.edu
            </a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <span class="opacity-70">Personal</span>
            <a class="email-link" href="mailto:wangjieyi0809@outlook.com">
                wangjieyi0809@outlook.com
            </a>
        </li>
    </ul>

